      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Reactions of Ln(NO3)3·xH2O, 2-hydroxybenzophenone (Hhbzp) and Et3N in a 1:1:1 ratio in 98% EtOH gave golden yellow solutions from which yellow crystalline powders of [Eu9(OH)10(hbzp)16](NO3) (1) were isolated. The cluster is isostructural with the crystallographically characterized Tb analogue as shown by elemental analyses, PXRD and IR. Typical isolated yields for the family are 60–65%.",
